-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 0050 — The rotation stops being one day long.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- 0047 built the schema and seeded exactly one narration — the one the old
-- `DAILY_HADITH` constant carried — leaving the rotation one day long until
-- someone supplied more. This is that supply: 390 further narrations, all
-- English, bringing the total to 391.
--
-- ── Source ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- fawazahmed0/hadith-api (cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/fawazahmed0/hadith-api@1), an
-- open mirror of standard published English translations of the hadith
-- collections, keyed by the same book/hadith numbering the collections
-- themselves use. Not machine-translated, not generated: fetched as English
-- text and imported as-is. Spot-checked against the single most verifiable
-- entry in the corpus before trusting the rest of it — Bukhari 1 ("Actions
-- are judged by intentions...") matched the well-known standard translation
-- word for word.
--
-- Two curated forty-hadith collections in full — 40 Hadith Nawawi (42
-- narrations) and 40 Hadith Qudsi (40) — plus three broadly beneficial books
-- of Sahih al-Bukhari in full: Belief (51), Knowledge (76), and Ar-Riqaq, "To
-- Make the Heart Tender" (181). Chosen for being foundational and reflective
-- rather than procedural fiqh, which is a better match for a card meant to
-- open the app than the books on inheritance shares or trade contracts would
-- have been.
--
-- ── Still no translation, on purpose ───────────────────────────────────────
-- English only, exactly as 0047 requires: nothing here is machine-translated
-- into the app's five other locales. A locale with no hadith text of its own
-- keeps falling back to English on the card. Non-English translations of
-- these narrations arrive the same way English did — from a published
-- edition, entered by hand at /admin/hadiths — never generated.
--
-- ── Order ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- `position` is a fixed pseudo-random interleaving (seeded shuffle) rather
-- than the source order, so the rotation does not run through all 181 Riqaq
-- narrations back to back before reaching Knowledge. It starts at 1 — the
-- 0047 seed keeps position 0 and stays first.
--
-- Verified after applying, directly against the live database: 391 hadiths
-- total (the 0047 seed plus these 390), zero duplicate references, zero rows
-- without an English translation, and `daily_hadith()` still returning
-- exactly one narration with real text and a correct reference.

